OPAL

Performance-first remote desktop for Linux, Apple Silicon macOS, and Windows.
Tailscale is required on both computers. OPAL runs its own authenticated, end-to-end encrypted direct session over the tailnet.

LINUX
=====

Fedora / Fedora Asahi:

  sudo dnf install -y gcc-c++ make git pkgconf-pkg-config SDL3-devel openssl-devel ffmpeg ffmpeg-devel pipewire pipewire-devel pipewire-pulseaudio libportal libportal-devel xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Arch / CachyOS:

  sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel git pkgconf sdl3 openssl ffmpeg pipewire pipewire-pulse libportal xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Debian / Ubuntu:

  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y build-essential git pkg-config libsdl3-dev libssl-dev ffmpeg libavformat-dev libavcodec-dev libavutil-dev libswresample-dev libswscale-dev libpipewire-0.3-dev libportal-dev pipewire pipewire-pulse xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-kde wl-clipboard curl

Tailscale:

  curl -fsSL https://tailscale.com/install.sh | sh
  sudo tailscale up

Build:

  git clone https://github.com/xt9y/OPAL.git
  cd OPAL
  make -j"$(nproc)"
  sudo make install


MACOS
=====

Requirements: Apple Silicon, macOS 13+, Xcode Command Line Tools, Homebrew, and Tailscale.

Install Tailscale from:

  https://tailscale.com/download/mac

Open Tailscale and sign in, then:

  xcode-select --install
  brew install pkg-config sdl3 openssl@3 ffmpeg git
  git clone https://github.com/xt9y/OPAL.git
  cd OPAL
  make
  make install

Do not run sudo make install on macOS.

Hosting requires Screen & System Audio Recording permission for OPAL and Accessibility permission for opal-input.


WINDOWS
=======

Requirements: Windows 10+, MSYS2 UCRT64 for building, and Tailscale.

Install Tailscale from:

  https://tailscale.com/download/windows

Run the installer and sign in from the Tailscale system-tray app.

In MSYS2 UCRT64:

  pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-toolchain mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-pkgconf mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-SDL3 mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-openssl mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-ffmpeg make git
  git clone https://github.com/xt9y/OPAL.git
  cd OPAL
  make
  make verify
  make install


VIRTUAL MONITORS
================

Linux:

No separate virtual-display driver or service is required. OPAL creates KWin/Wayland virtual outputs at runtime. Use KDE Plasma on Wayland. Headless hosting requires kwin_wayland, plasmashell, Xwayland, PipeWire, and a working user D-Bus/systemd session. sudo make install installs OPAL's user services.

macOS:

No separate virtual-display driver or service is required. OPAL creates CGVirtualDisplay displays at runtime. Install OPAL normally with make install and grant the hosting permissions listed above.

Windows:

The OPAL virtual monitor uses an Indirect Display Driver and requires Visual Studio, the Windows SDK, and the Windows Driver Kit.

In PowerShell, install the Microsoft WDK toolset:

  winget configure -f 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/Windows-driver-samples/main/_wdk_utils/winget/configs/wdk-vscommunity.dsc.yaml'

Then reopen MSYS2 UCRT64 in the OPAL repository and run:

  make install

make install automatically builds and installs the OPAL virtual display driver and may request administrator permission. Restart Windows if OPAL reports that a restart is required.

To build only the Windows virtual-display package:

  make windows-headless

The virtual display is removed together with OPAL by:

  make uninstall


RUN
===

  opal
  opal select
  opal doctor
  OPAL_DEBUG=1 opal

The first connection uses the host connection code and pairing password. Saved hosts reuse their identity and learned Tailscale address on later connections.
